<%# HTML-body sink view. `raw` is used on purpose here: a sink never escapes
    anything itself, so both twins of a minimal pair share this exact view
    fragment and the cell's transform region alone decides whether the value
    reaching this line was already escaped (mirrors php_laravel's own
    html_body_echo.blade.php.j2 -- see that emitter's modules.py docstring,
    decision 2, for the full rationale this stack reuses). Rendered inside the
    ForgeCart layout (app/views/layouts/application.html.erb, CC-LAB-0245). %>
{% if page_title %}
<% content_for :title, "{{ page_title }} - ForgeCart" %>
<h1>{{ page_title }}</h1>
{% endif %}
<div class="cell-output"><%= raw @value %></div>
